From c3dc3f610456a4ebf0a1f7cab2da8bac16feacdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakshman <lakshman@lakshman-GG9LQ90J61.local>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 11:30:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(22-04): publish bounded compatibility catalog and MV2
 observation

- Add prometheus_extension_compatibility_catalog.{h,cc}: a closed,
  compiled five-row evidence catalog (category/fixture/version/SHA-256,
  manifest version, install source, Prometheus build, Chromium revision,
  regular/Private mode exercised, actions, Verified/Degraded/Unsupported
  result, bounded limitation, evidence artifact) plus a WebUI-shaped
  projector and a closed-catalog validator.
- Replace the fixed "unsupported"/"No verified fixture" Parity Matrix
  placeholder in prometheus_web_ui.cc with the real catalog projection.
- Add ManifestV2PinnedPolicyObservation to
  prometheus_extension_fixtures_browsertest.cc: loads the observation-only
  mv2_observation fixture through the ordinary UnpackedInstaller path with
  no MV2 allowance helper or verification bypass, and records the
  native accepted/rejected result plus one stable reason code both as
  gtest properties and directly to a file for verify script consumption.
  On this pinned revision, unpacked MV2 load is natively rejected
  (reason: unpacked_load_failed) -- observed, not asserted.
- Add the new mv2_observation MV2 manifest/background fixture, kept
  entirely separate from the five MV3 acceptance fixtures.
- Fix three pre-existing dead/incorrect BUILD.gn dependency labels
  uncovered while wiring the new catalog target (dangling
  //chrome/browser/ui/views/side_panel/extensions, non-existent
  prometheus_page_action_dispatcher/page_element_reader/page_snapshot
  targets that are actually files inside prometheus_page_adapter, and
  //chrome/browser/ui/tabs:tab_features which is actually :impl).
